3.1. The wake-closure phenomenon
The HPGA type nozzle configuration contains the basic flow characteristics seen in air-breathing truncated plug nozzle studies by Sule and Mueller [10] for ‘altitude-compensating’ operation. In order to understand the wake-closure phenomenon, and to answer the cause of the apparent augmented particle refinement during melt atomization across the WCP, events of the gas dynamics in the recirculation zone and the surrounding gas field had to be modeled. (In the pa


